When the head of the chain matches, C sets [38;5;10metab[h] = NULL[0m instead of [38;5;10metab[h] = p->next[0m. This means it drops all other edges in the same hash bucket. The Rust code has a comment about this but let me verify the Rust code matches this behavior.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Looking at the Rust [38;5;10mdel()[0m:[0m[0m
[1mrust
