}
[0m[0m[0m
[0m[0m
When [38;5;10mtake()[0m is called, it takes the entire head node. But the head node's [38;5;10mnext[0m field (which contains the rest of the chain) gets dropped with it. So the Rust code DOES match the C bug — the rest of the chain is dropped.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
